# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The job proves the machine before it deploys.** [assert_architecture.sh](../../../scripts/github/runner/assert_architecture.sh) compares `uname -m` against the assigned value and fails the row on a mismatch. Without it, a label that stops resolving to arm64 hardware would report every arm64 row green from an amd64 machine, which is the exact failure the axis exists to rule out."
msgstr "**Kazi inaonyesha mashine kabla ya kutumia.** [assert_architecture.sh](../../../scripts/github/runner/assert_architecture.sh) Kulinganisha `uname -m` dhidi ya thamani iliyotolewa na kushindwa mstari kwenye mechi. Bila kufanya hivyo, maandiko ambayo yanaacha kutatua kwa mkono64 Vyombo vya habari vinaripoti kila mkono64 Rangi ya kijani kutoka amd64 mashine, ambayo ni kushindwa halisi mhimili ipo ya utawala nje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The matrix carries the runner label, and `runs-on` reads it.** The entry gains `architecture` and `runner`; [pools.py](../../../utils/github/variant/pools.py) owns the mapping (`amd64` → `ubuntu-latest`, `arm64` → `ubuntu-24.04-arm`). An architecture without a label is a build error rather than a row that lands on the wrong hardware with an empty `runs-on`."
msgstr "**Kwa upande mwingine, mvuvi huyo anashikilia rekodi ya mchezaji huyo, na `runs-on` Soma hii.** Mafanikio ya kuingia `architecture` Aidha, na `runner`; [pools.py](../../../utils/github/variant/pools.py) Kuwa na ramani (`amd64` kuwa `ubuntu-latest`, Kwa hivyo, `arm64` kuwa `ubuntu-24.04-arm`)Usanifu bila lebo ni kosa la kujenga badala ya mstari unaoweka kwenye vifaa vibaya na tupu `runs-on`..."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The migration is blocked on a transport gap, and the credential half of it is already built.** The adapter presented its upstream credential only as a header (`ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY` → `Authorization: Bearer …`) while Baserow keys its endpoint by URL segment, so `policy.upstream_url` now splices an optional `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_KEY` and `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_SUFFIX` into the upstream URL, delivered through the same `upstream.env` file. With neither variable set it returns the base URL unchanged, which is why the fourteen existing providers are untouched."
msgstr "**Uhamiaji umezuiliwa kwenye pengo la usafiri, na nusu yake tayari imejengwa.** Mtafsiri aliwasilisha fomu yake ya juu kama kichwa tu. (`ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY` kuwa `Authorization: Bearer …`) Wakati akiwa Baserow Inafungua sehemu ya mwisho ya URL, hivyo `policy.upstream_url` Sasa ni wakati wa kuchagua `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_KEY` Aidha, na `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_SUFFIX` Kuingia kwenye URL, iliyotolewa kwa njia sawa `upstream.env` ya faili. Kwa kuweka hakuna tofauti inarudi URL ya msingi isiyobadilika, ndiyo sababu watoa huduma wa sasa wa kumi na nne hawajaguswa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The platform does not deploy one all-powerful OpenAPI-to-MCP process.** It provides one reusable, immutable adapter implementation and instantiates it once per provider application or per equally isolated trust domain. Each instance attaches only to the provider's own network, receives only that provider's least-privileged credential, exposes a distinct endpoint, and stays addressable by the provider's `application_id`. Every exposed provider remains a separate logical MCP server even when a common implementation serves it, which preserves the mapping between `roles/<provider-application-id>/mcp`, the client connection, the upstream credential, the tool allowlist and the audit record."
msgstr "**Mfumo huu haujumuishi mchakato wa OpenAPI-to-MCP.** Inatoa moja ya utekelezaji wa adapta inayoweza kubadilika, usiobadilika na unaiweka mara moja kwa maombi ya mtoa huduma au kwa kikoa cha pekee cha uaminifu. Kila mfano unaunganisha tu kwenye mtandao wa mtoa huduma mwenyewe, hupokea tu uaminifu mdogo wa mtoa huduma, unafunua mwisho tofauti, na unakaa kushughulikia na mtoa huduma wa huduma. `application_id`. Kila mtoa huduma aliye wazi anabakia seva tofauti ya mantiki ya MCP hata wakati utekelezaji wa kawaida unatumikia, ambayo huhifadhi ramani kati ya `roles/<provider-application-id>/mcp`, uhusiano mteja, upstream credential, chombo cha kuruhusu na rekodi ya ukaguzi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The pools are narrowable per run.** The `distros` and `filesystem` inputs default to empty, which means every declared value. Narrowing is for chasing one distribution or one filesystem."
msgstr "**Miguu ni nyembamba kwa kukimbia.** Kwa kuwa `distros` Aidha, na `filesystem` Inaleta default kwa tupu, ambayo inamaanisha kila thamani iliyotangazwa. Narrowing ni kwa ajili ya Chasing usambazaji mmoja au mfumo wa faili moja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The raft volume is `nfs: false` and the service carries `placement: manager`.**"
msgstr "**Kiwango cha raft ni `nfs: false` Huduma ya usafiri `placement: manager`...**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The recovery key is the way back in.** ``bao operator init`` issues it once and nothing reissues it, which is what makes it useful — it is the only authority here that does not rotate. It is persisted through ``sys-token-store`` (``DIR_SECRETS``, backed up, and it survives both ``MODE_RESET`` and a replaced manager, each of which takes ``.applied.json`` with it). When neither the inventory AppRole nor the recorded one is accepted, ``tasks/utils/recover.yml`` mints a root token from it and re-pins the AppRole. It cannot decrypt the store — only the seal key can — so it is not a substitute for backing up the inventory."
msgstr "**Njia ya kurudi ni njia ya kurudi.** ``bao operator init`` Inashughulikia mara moja na hakuna kitu kinachorudisha, ambayo ndiyo inafanya kuwa muhimu - ni mamlaka pekee hapa ambayo haizunguki. imeendelea kupitia ``sys-token-store`` (``DIR_SECRETS``, kwa pamoja, na hivyo kuendelea kuishi kwa ``MODE_RESET`` kuwa na kiongozi ambaye kila mmoja ana ``.applied.json`` Pamoja na hayo). Na kama huna cha kuandika wala kuandika. ``tasks/utils/recover.yml`` Kisha, safisha uso wako vizuri, tumia cream ya greasi. Haiwezi kufuta duka - tu ufunguo wa muhuri unaweza - kwa hivyo sio mbadala wa kuunga mkono hesabu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The recovery key is the way back in.** `bao operator init` issues it once and nothing reissues it, which is what makes it useful — it is the only authority here that does not rotate. It is persisted through `sys-token-store` (`DIR_SECRETS`, backed up, and it survives both `MODE_RESET` and a replaced manager, each of which takes `.applied.json` with it). When neither the inventory AppRole nor the recorded one is accepted, `tasks/utils/recover.yml` mints a root token from it and re-pins the AppRole. It cannot decrypt the store — only the seal key can — so it is not a substitute for backing up the inventory."
msgstr "**Njia ya kurudi ni njia ya kurudi.** `bao operator init` Inashughulikia mara moja na hakuna kitu kinachorudisha, ambayo ndiyo inafanya kuwa muhimu - ni mamlaka pekee hapa ambayo haizunguki. imeendelea kupitia `sys-token-store` (`DIR_SECRETS`, kwa pamoja, na hivyo kuendelea kuishi kwa `MODE_RESET` kuwa na kiongozi ambaye kila mmoja ana `.applied.json` Pamoja na hayo). Na kama huna cha kuandika wala kuandika. `tasks/utils/recover.yml` Kisha, safisha uso wako vizuri, tumia cream ya greasi. Haiwezi kufuta duka - tu ufunguo wa muhuri unaweza - kwa hivyo sio mbadala wa kuunga mkono hesabu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The role tree is the audit.** Every fact about a role's MCP surface lives in its own `meta/services.yml`; no separate artifact duplicates it."
msgstr "**Kamati ya utendaji ni Kamati ya Ukaguzi.** Kila ukweli kuhusu sehemu ya MCP huishi katika sehemu yake mwenyewe. `meta/services.yml`; Hakuna njia ya mkato ya kufanya hivyo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The router is a LiteLLM pre-call hook, not a semantic router.** The hook summarizes the request, filters the gateway's own model list down to the routes that can serve it, and picks one. LiteLLM's built-in `auto_router` is explicitly rejected: it routes by embedding similarity to example utterances, which answers \"what is this about\" rather than \"which model can serve this\", and it pulls in the `semantic-router` extra plus an embedding backend the gateway does not otherwise need."
msgstr "**Router ni ndoano ya kabla ya simu, sio router ya semantic.** ndoano muhtasari ombi, filters mlango mwenyewe mfano orodha chini ya njia ambayo inaweza kutumika, na picks moja. Nyumba ya LiteLLM `auto_router` ni wazi kukataliwa: ni njia kwa kuingiza kufanana na matamshi ya mfano, ambayo majibu \"Nini hii kuhusu\" Badala yake badala ya \"Mfumo gani unaweza kutumika\"Na kwa upande wake Balozi wa `semantic-router` ziada pamoja na kuingizwa backend lango haina vinginevyo haja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The router is an alias beside the default, and it fails loud.** The gateway publishes one additional `model_name` (`auto`). `LITELLM_CHAT_MODEL` and every existing alias keep resolving exactly as they do today, and a consumer opts in by naming `auto`."
msgstr "**Njia ni pana, na njia ni pana.** Kituo hicho kinatoa taarifa zaidi `model_name` (`auto`)... `LITELLM_CHAT_MODEL` na kila alias zilizopo zinaendelea kutatua hasa kama wanavyofanya leo, na watumiaji huchagua kwa kutaja `auto`..."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The runtime identity differs.** act sets `ACT=true`, so `detect_gha_act()` in [runtime.py](../../../../utils/env/runtime.py) resolves `INFINITO_RUNNING_ON_GITHUB=false` where a real runner resolves `true`. Anything keyed off that fact behaves differently, and act cannot prove a fix to it either way."
msgstr "**Utambulisho wa muda hutofautiana.** Utekelezaji wa `ACT=true`, Kwa hivyo, kwa `detect_gha_act()` Ndani ya [runtime.py](../../../../utils/env/runtime.py) Uamuzi wa `INFINITO_RUNNING_ON_GITHUB=false` ambapo mshindi wa kweli `true`. Kila kitu kilichotokana na ukweli huo hufanya tofauti, na kitendo hakiwezi kuthibitisha kurekebisha kwa njia yoyote."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The seal key is the whole ballgame.** The ``static`` seal wraps the raft root key with ``secrets.credentials.seal_key``, injected as ``env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY``. A backup of the raft volume is **undecryptable without it**, and ``svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`` does not cover it — the encrypted inventory is its only home, so back the inventory up accordingly. It is pinned ``rotatable: false``: the static seal carries one generation of slack, and spending that every deploy makes any skipped generation unrecoverable. Rotate it deliberately by changing the inventory value; ``openbao.hcl.j2`` then emits the ``previous_key``/``previous_key_id`` pair, the node unseals with the old key and rewraps to the new one."
msgstr "**Mpira wa kikapu ni mchezo wote wa mpira.** Kwa kuwa ``static`` Simba yatwaa taji la Ligi Kuu Bara ``secrets.credentials.seal_key``, Kuingizwa kama ``env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY``. Backup ya kiasi cha raft ni **bila mpangilio bila mpangilio**Aidha, na ``svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`` Haijalishi - hesabu iliyofichwa ni nyumba yake pekee, hivyo nyuma hesabu ipasavyo. Ilikuwa imefungwa ``rotatable: false``: muhuri tuli hubeba kizazi kimoja cha slack, na matumizi ambayo kila kupeleka hufanya kizazi chochote kilichoruka kisichowezekana. Badilisha kwa makusudi kwa kubadilisha thamani ya hesabu; ``openbao.hcl.j2`` Baada ya hayo, ``previous_key``Kwa hivyo``previous_key_id`` jozi, node unseals na ufunguo wa zamani na rewraps kwa moja mpya."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The seal key is the whole ballgame.** The `static` seal wraps the raft root key with `secrets.credentials.seal_key`, injected as `env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY`. A backup of the raft volume is **undecryptable without it**, and `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local` does not cover it — the encrypted inventory is its only home, so back the inventory up accordingly. It is pinned `rotatable: false`: the static seal carries one generation of slack, and spending that every deploy makes any skipped generation unrecoverable. Rotate it deliberately by changing the inventory value; `openbao.hcl.j2` then emits the `previous_key`/`previous_key_id` pair, the node unseals with the old key and rewraps to the new one."
msgstr "**Mpira wa kikapu ni mchezo wote wa mpira.** Kwa kuwa `static` Simba yatwaa taji la Ligi Kuu Bara `secrets.credentials.seal_key`, Kuingizwa kama `env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY`. Backup ya kiasi cha raft ni **bila mpangilio bila mpangilio**Aidha, na `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local` Haijalishi - hesabu iliyofichwa ni nyumba yake pekee, hivyo nyuma hesabu ipasavyo. Ilikuwa imefungwa `rotatable: false`: muhuri tuli hubeba kizazi kimoja cha slack, na matumizi ambayo kila kupeleka hufanya kizazi chochote kilichoruka kisichowezekana. Badilisha kwa makusudi kwa kubadilisha thamani ya hesabu; `openbao.hcl.j2` Baada ya hayo, `previous_key`Kwa hivyo`previous_key_id` jozi, node unseals na ufunguo wa zamani na rewraps kwa moja mpya."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The version has to fit.** The dump states which server it came out of, in its own header — `-- Dumped from database version 17.11` for postgres, `-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB` for mariadb. That is compared against the running engine before the pre-clean touches anything. Restoring forward across a major version is the upgrade path and stays allowed; backward is refused, because a newer dump uses syntax an older server rejects and the schema would already be dropped by then. The version is deliberately not kept in `databases.csv`: that file is written at seed time and would state the version deployed back then, not the one the dump came from — and a generation copied to another host carries its header along, a csv row does not."
msgstr "**Tafsiri inapaswa kuwa sahihi.** Kwa upande wake Mbunge wa Jimbo la Ludewa Mhe. `-- Dumped from database version 17.11` kwa hisani ya RaiaMwema `-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB` kwa hisani ya RaiaMwema. Hii ni sawa na kupanda mbegu kabla ya kupanda. Kurejesha mbele katika toleo kuu ni njia ya kuboresha na kukaa kuruhusiwa; nyuma ni kukataa, kwa sababu dump ya karibu inatumia syntax server mzee anakataa na schema itakuwa tayari imeshuka na wakati huo. Tafsiri hiyo haijawekwa katika `databases.csv`: Faili hiyo imeandikwa wakati wa mbegu na itasema toleo lililotumika wakati huo, sio moja ya dump imetoka - na kizazi kilichonakiliwa kwa mwenyeji mwingine hubeba kichwa chake pamoja, mstari wa csv hau."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The version has to fit.** The dump states which server it came out of, in its own header — ``-- Dumped from database version 17.11`` for postgres, ``-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB`` for mariadb. That is compared against the running engine before the pre-clean touches anything. Restoring forward across a major version is the upgrade path and stays allowed; backward is refused, because a newer dump uses syntax an older server rejects and the schema would already be dropped by then. The version is deliberately not kept in ``databases.csv``: that file is written at seed time and would state the version deployed back then, not the one the dump came from — and a generation copied to another host carries its header along, a csv row does not."
msgstr "**Tafsiri inapaswa kuwa sahihi.** Kwa upande wake Mbunge wa Jimbo la Ludewa Mhe. ``-- Dumped from database version 17.11`` kwa hisani ya RaiaMwema ``-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB`` kwa hisani ya RaiaMwema. Hii ni sawa na kupanda mbegu kabla ya kupanda. Kurejesha mbele katika toleo kuu ni njia ya kuboresha na kukaa kuruhusiwa; nyuma ni kukataa, kwa sababu dump ya karibu inatumia syntax server mzee anakataa na schema itakuwa tayari imeshuka na wakati huo. Tafsiri hiyo haijawekwa katika ``databases.csv``: Faili hiyo imeandikwa wakati wa mbegu na itasema toleo lililotumika wakati huo, sio moja ya dump imetoka - na kizazi kilichonakiliwa kwa mwenyeji mwingine hubeba kichwa chake pamoja, mstari wa csv hau."

