# translation-rejected: **https kwenye onion IdP - iliyochunguzwa na
# kurekebishwa, usibadilishe tena.** Ugunduzi wa OIDC / RFC 8414 Unahitaji
# toleo la https, na onion-exclusive Keycloak Hakuna mtu, hivyo vitabu vya
# wateja vikali kukataa. Kutumikia TLS kwenye onion imefungwa kwenye mambo
# manne ya kujitegemea, kwa utaratibu huu: (1)
# `roles/svc-net-tor/templates/torrc.j2` Kuchapisha tu `HiddenServicePort 80`,
# Hakuna sehemu yoyote inayotangaza 443 Ndani ya `ports.public`Kwa
# hivyo`ports.local`, Kwa hivyo, kwa `lookup('tor_ports')` Haiwezi kamwe kutoa
# - flipping TLS hufanya kwanza Keycloak kwa ujumla wake, kwa sababu
# `nginx_ssl_header.j2` Moja ikiwa ni pamoja na bandari 80 ya kutoweka; (2)
# `roles/sys-front-tls-selfsigned/tasks/00_core.yml` Anaandika CN
# isiyohifadhiwa, ambayo inazunguka X.509ya ya ya 64Bonyeza kwenye A 62ya ya
# ya3 ya ya ya - `group_vars/all/02_tls.yml` Hii ni kwa ajili ya kulinda
# mizizi na mahali pengine popote. (3) `nginx_ssl_header.j2` Hutoa HSTS katika
# tawi moja, na vivinjari kutoa hakuna click-through juu ya HSTS mwenyeji na
# mnyororo untrusted, hivyo locks binafsi saini muda watumiaji halisi nje
# wakati kukaa asiyeonekana kwa Playwright ya. `ignoreHTTPSErrors`; (4)
# Inabadilisha watumiaji wa libcurl ya sifuri, kwa sababu RFC 7686 Kukataa
# hufanyika kwa jina la azimio na inategemea mpango. Kufungia inahitaji CA
# ambayo inashughulikia v3 `.onion` (Kura ya maoni CA/B Forum 144) Kununua,
# sio kodi. Hadi wakati huo, marekebisho ya kila mtumiaji yanasimama: wakala
# wa SOCKS kwa wateja wa libcurl. Kwa hivyo, hakuna haja ya kuwa na wasiwasi
# juu ya hilo - ni jukumu la wazi.
msgid "**https on the onion IdP — investigated and REJECTED, do not re-derive.** OIDC Discovery / RFC 8414 want an https issuer, and an onion-exclusive Keycloak has none, so strict client libraries refuse it. Serving TLS on the onion is blocked on four independent things, in this order: (1) `roles/svc-net-tor/templates/torrc.j2` publishes only `HiddenServicePort 80`, and no role declares 443 in `ports.public`/`ports.local`, so `lookup('tor_ports')` can never emit it — flipping TLS on first makes Keycloak unreachable over Tor entirely, because `nginx_ssl_header.j2` is one if/else and port 80 disappears; (2) `roles/sys-front-tls-selfsigned/tasks/00_core.yml` writes an unguarded CN, which overflows X.509's 64-byte cap on a 62-char v3 onion — `group_vars/all/02_tls.yml` already guards exactly this for the root CA and nowhere else; (3) `nginx_ssl_header.j2` emits HSTS in the same branch, and browsers offer no click-through on an HSTS host with an untrusted chain, so a self-signed interim locks real users out while staying invisible to Playwright's `ignoreHTTPSErrors`; (4) it fixes zero libcurl consumers, because RFC 7686 refusal happens at name resolution and is scheme-independent. Unblocking needs a CA that issues for v3 `.onion` (HARICA, CA/B Forum ballot 144) — procurement, not code. Until then the per-consumer fixes stand: SOCKS proxy for libcurl clients. peertube is no longer among them - it is a clearnet-only role."
