# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Still open: MCP calls carrying that identity, and the obstacle is upstream rather than a piece of this platform nobody wrote yet. [ADR 0003](../architecture/decisions/0003-mcp-surface-per-provider.md) already fixes the bar: `auth_subject: user` may be set only after the exact client and server prove authorization-code or token-exchange behaviour, token refresh, audience binding, revocation and expiry. No MCP provider deployed here clears it — every server role authenticates as one `service_account`, because that is what its upstream offers — so `auth_subject: user` has nothing to resolve against. Meeting the bar means a provider gaining per-user OAuth upstream, not a credential model this repository can add on its own."
msgstr "Bado wazi: MCP wito kubeba utambulisho huo, na kikwazo ni upstream badala ya kipande cha jukwaa hili hakuna mtu aliandika bado. [ADR ya 0003](../architecture/decisions/0003-mcp-surface-per-provider.md) Sasa unaweza kubadilisha bar: `auth_subject: user` Inaweza kuwekwa tu baada ya mteja halisi na seva kuthibitisha msimbo wa idhini au tabia ya kubadilisha ishara, kuburudisha ishara, kufungwa kwa watazamaji, kukasirisha na expiry. Hakuna mtoa huduma wa MCP aliyeweka hapa anaisafisha - kila jukumu la seva linathibitisha kama moja `service_account`, Hii ni kwa sababu hii ndiyo njia ya pekee ya kufanya hivyo – `auth_subject: user` Hakuna kitu cha kupinga. Kukutana na bar ina maana mtoa huduma kupata kwa kila mtumiaji OAuth upstream, si mfano credential hii hazina inaweza kuongeza peke yake."

