msgstr "Kwa mujibu wa `Corefile` Ni lazima kujenga ukuta na lazima kukaa katika `.gitignore`..."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The rendered fragment MUST start at the ``groups:`` item level (two-space indented ``- name: <group>`` entries), because it is concatenated into the single ``groups:`` list of the Prometheus rule file."
msgstr "Sehemu iliyotengwa inapaswa kuanza katika ``groups:`` Kiwango cha (Sehemu ya pili ya Indented ``- name: <group>`` Entries ya kuingia), Kwa sababu yeye ni katika umoja ``groups:`` Orodha ya Prometheus Kanuni ya faili."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The replay is a second deploy on the same runner, so the row it picks must be one the guide can actually deploy: the role has to be invokable, because that is what makes the documentation build give it a Production block, and the guide's own mode (``compose`` for a role that ships a stack, ``host`` for one installed onto the machine) has to be a mode the role runs and tests."
msgstr "Replay ni kupelekwa kwa pili kwenye mkimbiaji mmoja, kwa hivyo mstari unaochagua lazima uwe mmoja wa mwongozo unaoweza kupeleka: jukumu linapaswa kuwa lisilowezekana, kwa sababu hiyo ndio hufanya nyaraka zijenge kutoa kizuizi cha Uzalishaji, na mode ya mwongozo mwenyewe. (``compose`` Kwa upande mwingine, kwa upande wa meli, ``host`` Kwa mtu aliyewekwa kwenye mashine) Lazima kuwa njia ya kazi na majaribio."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The replay rides along on a deploy row of the sweep instead of holding a job of its own. [guide.py](../../../../../utils/roles/guide.py) marks one row per role:"
msgstr "Replay anaendesha pamoja juu ya mstari kupeleka sweep badala ya kufanya kazi yake mwenyewe. [guide.py](../../../../../utils/roles/guide.py) Weka mstari mmoja kwa kila jukumu:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The replay used to be a job of its own, picking one random role per run. It rides on a deploy row instead: the role's smallest variant among the rows this sweep actually deploys, marked with ``instructions`` (the mode the replay runs in) and a 📖 in the job title. :mod:`utils.roles.guide` decides which variant that is; this module is what turns the decision into matrix entries."
msgstr "Replay ilikuwa kazi yake mwenyewe, kuokota jukumu moja random kwa kila kukimbia. Inapanda kwenye mstari wa kupeleka badala yake: lahaja ndogo ya jukumu kati ya safu hii ya kufagia kwa kweli inachukua, alama na ``instructions`` (Jinsi ya kucheza Replay katika) Aidha, a 📖 katika jina la kazi. :mod:`utils.roles.guide` kuamua ni aina gani tofauti ambayo ni; moduli hii ni nini zamu uamuzi katika maingilio ya matrix."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The repo treats `biber` as the canonical non-admin RBAC fixture: the user is provisioned by `roles/svc-db-openldap` and exposed to specs via the `lookup('users', 'biber')` filter. ~19 role specs already consume `BIBER_USERNAME` / `BIBER_PASSWORD` from `roles/<role>/templates/playwright.env.j2` and drive at least one non-admin scenario (typically: SSO login via Keycloak, land on the expected post-login surface, optionally assert that admin-only UI is absent)."
msgstr "Repo yashughulikia `biber` Kama marekebisho yasiyo ya kanuni ya RBAC: mtumiaji hutolewa na `roles/svc-db-openldap` na kutoa taarifa kwa vyombo vya dola kupitia `lookup('users', 'biber')` ya filter.19 Vifaa vya ujenzi tayari vinatumia `BIBER_USERNAME` Kwa hivyo `BIBER_PASSWORD` Kutoka kwa `roles/<role>/templates/playwright.env.j2` na kuendesha angalau moja ya matukio yasiyo ya utawala (Kwa mfano: SSO login kupitia Keycloak, ardhi juu ya uso inatarajiwa baada yalogin, hiari kudai kwamba admin-tu UI haipo)..."

