msgid "[call-images-mirror-missing.yml](../../../../.github/workflows/call-images-mirror-missing.yml) mirrors any missing upstream images in parallel with the DNS tests so later deploy jobs pull from GHCR instead of Docker Hub, MCR, or other external registries. This shields CI from upstream rate limits, geo-blocking, and transient registry outages."
msgstr "[call-images-mirror-missing.yml](../../../../.github/workflows/call-images-mirror-missing.yml) Inaangalia picha zozote zinazokosekana sambamba na vipimo vya DNS hivyo baadaye kupeleka kazi kutoka kwa GHCR badala ya Docker Hub, MCR, au registries nyingine za nje. Hii ngao CI kutoka mipaka ya kiwango cha juu, kizuizi cha geo, na vikwazo vya usajili wa muda."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[call-orchestrator.yml](../../../../../.github/workflows/call-orchestrator.yml) compares `github.ref` for the same reason: a called workflow inherits the caller's ref, which is `refs/pull/<n>/merge` for a `pull_request` caller but `refs/heads/main` for a `pull_request_target` one. The `ci-orchestrator` job of `entry-pr-change-orchestrate.yml` is fenced to `github.event_name == 'pull_request'`, so the ref the orchestrator sees from that caller is always the merge ref; widening that fence would silently put fork runs into main's group."
msgstr "[call-orchestrator.yml](../../../../../.github/workflows/call-orchestrator.yml) Kulinganisha `github.ref` Kwa sababu hiyo hiyo: kazi inayoitwa inarithi ref ya mwombaji, ambayo ni `refs/pull/<n>/merge` Kwa ajili ya A `pull_request` simu lakini `refs/heads/main` Kwa ajili ya A `pull_request_target` moja. Kwa kuwa `ci-orchestrator` Kazi ya `entry-pr-change-orchestrate.yml` Kuwa tayari `github.event_name == 'pull_request'`, hivyo ref orchestrator anaona kutoka kwa simu hiyo ni daima kuunganisha ref; kupanua kwamba uzio ingekuwa kimya kuweka ngome anaendesha katika kundi kuu."

